+``--demuxer-cache-unselected-subtitles=<seconds>``
+    Keep packets for unselected subtitle streams that are embedded in the same
+    demuxer as audio or video (default: 0, disabled). The value specifies how
+    much subtitle history to retain behind the playback position. This can make
+    switching embedded subtitle tracks avoid a demuxer refresh seek.
+
+    Subtitle-only demuxers, such as external subtitle files, are not affected.
+    Enabling this option increases demuxing work and memory use. If retained
+    packets do not cover the requested position, track selection falls back to
+    the normal refresh-seek behavior.
+
+``--demuxer-cache-unselected-subtitles-max-bytes=<bytesize>``
+    Limit the combined packet memory used by
+    ``--demuxer-cache-unselected-subtitles`` (default: 16 MiB). The limit is
+    shared across eligible embedded subtitle streams and cache ranges. If the
+    limit is too small for a stream, old packets are discarded and switching to
+    it may use the normal refresh-seek fallback.
+
 ``--demuxer-thread=<yes|no>``
     Run the demuxer in a separate thread, and let it prefetch a certain amount
     of packets (default: yes). Having this enabled leads to smoother playback,
